	(text "TI DN024 / SWRA227E meandering monopole, dual band 868 + 2440 MHz.\n\nUnlike the SWRA117D inverted-F, this antenna is NOT a 50 ohm part: the\nnote requires a pi network at the feed and gives its values, because the\nground plane geometry sets the antenna's impedance.\n\nTable 3, dual band BOM:   Z61 NC   Z62 3.9 pF series   Z63 NC\n  -> measured SWR 1.2 at 868 MHz and 1.6 at 2.44 GHz\nTable 2, single band 868: Z61 2.7 pF   Z62 1.8 nH series   Z63 NC\n  -> SWR 1.1, but it also needs L4 shortened, which the note does not\n     dimension, so that variant is not an exact copy of Table 1.\n\nZ61 and Z63 are laid out and left unfitted on purpose: the note's reason\nfor the network is to have somewhere to compensate detuning caused by\nplastic encapsulation and objects near the antenna.\n\nGround plane 43 x 63 mm - the size the published match belongs to. A\nlarger plane needs L4 reduced or the match recalculated (section 3).\nNo ground plane, no copper and no components under or beside the\nantenna; 2.5 mm clear either side, as the reference board leaves."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 112 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3c94fb9d-15da-51cf-9a52-167668aa1245")
	)
